108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (Artificial intelligence tools have become widely used across different fields, yet choosing the right tool can be challenging due to the large number of available options and the differences in their features, skill requirements, and pricing models. This project aims to address this challenge by developing an AI-based recommendation system that helps users identify the most suitable AI tool based on three key criteria: the type of task they want to perform, their skill level, and their available budget.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (The importance of this problem lies in the growing reliance on AI technologies in education, business, and everyday tasks. As the number of AI tools continues to increase, users often struggle to determine which tool best fits their needs. A recommendation system like the one implemented in this project simplifies the decision-making process, saves time, and promotes more effective use of AI resources. By guiding users toward appropriate tools, the system supports better learning outcomes, enhances productivity, and contributes to the broader adoption of AI in society.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
