132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (When the user interacts with the system, they provide three inputs: the task type they want to perform, their skill level, and their available budget. Once these inputs are entered, the system begins processing them by searching the knowledge base for tools that match the given criteria. If an exact match is found, the system recommends the corresponding tool. If no perfect match exists, the inference engine applies alternative rules to identify tools that share similar characteristics, ensuring that the user still receives helpful suggestions. This logical flow demonstrates how the system transforms user inputs into meaningful recommendations through structured reasoning.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
